Z||000002||Songman||12-31-2000||08:48 PM||||Buy the car and leave it there, but register it in your state. That is what I do. If you ever get pulled over and have a car registered in one state and a driver's license from another it will be a long explanation to the officer. Nothing illegal about it but it sure does make it easier to explain. <P>I keep some of my cars down in GA but they are all registered in TN. And thanks to TN laws I don't have to keep insurance on the ones I hardly ever drive. GA requires any car that is registered to have insurance no matter how much it is driven.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||01-01-2001||02:26 PM||||all my vehicles are registered at THEIR place of residence.  This makes life convenient as my 57 vw (which drives 100 miles a year if that)is in Wisconsin where insurance is not required pending you have a good driving record so mr insurance man told me.||||reg||1
